message.content:
The main bug is that the loop compares each element to `max_val` instead of to the value of the current streak. That means a streak of any value that is not already the “max” value never gets counted.

For `[2, 2, 1, 1, 1]`:

- `max_val` starts as `2`.
- The first two `2`s are counted.
- The following `1`s are never accumulated, because `data[i] == max_val` is false for them.
- The final streak is also never compared to the maximum, because the code only updates `max_count` when it sees a value different from `max_val`.

So the code effectively only tracks streaks of the initial value, and it also misses the last streak.

<solution language="rust" verdict="fix">
fn longest_streak(data: &Vec<i32>) -> (i32, usize) {
    let mut max_val = data[0];
    let mut max_count: usize = 1;
    let mut current_val = data[0];
    let mut current_count: usize = 1;

    for i in 1..data.len() {
        if data[i] == current_val {
            current_count += 1;
        } else {
            current_val = data[i];
            current_count = 1;
        }

        if current_count > max_count {
            max_val = current_val;
            max_count = current_count;
        }
    }

    (max_val, max_count)
}
</solution>

