The crash is on this line:

```js
const city = order.shipping_address.city;
```

That assumes `order.shipping_address` is always an object. In production, at least some orders have `order.shipping_address` as `undefined` or `null`, so JavaScript throws:

```text
Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'city')
```

It likely works locally because your local test orders always include a shipping address.

The fix is to safely access the nested property:

